 <body>
   <main class="page">
     <header>
       <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
       <p>Answers to the most common questions about our favorite mysterious roommates.</p>
     </header>

     <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
           <strong>Why do cats sleep so much?</strong>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details">
           <p>Cats conserve energy for short bursts of activity, so a long nap schedule is completely normal. A cozy cat is usually a healthy cat.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
           <strong>Why does my cat bring me toys?</strong>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details">
           <p>Your cat may be sharing a prize, practicing hunting behavior, or simply showing affection. It is a compliment, even if it arrives at 3 a.m.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
           <strong>Do cats like routines?</strong>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details">
           <p>Yes. Cats usually feel safest when meals, play, and quiet time happen predictably. Small routines help them stay relaxed and confident.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
           <strong>How can I tell if my cat is happy?</strong>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details">
           <p>Look for slow blinks, relaxed posture, steady appetite, grooming, and calm curiosity. A cat choosing to sit near you is also a strong hint.</p>
         </div>
       </div>
     </section>
   </main>

   <script>
     document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((example) => {
       const button = example.querySelector(".question");
       const details = example.querySelector(".details");

       button.addEventListener("click", () => {
         const isOpen = example.classList.toggle("open");
         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(isOpen));
         details.hidden = !isOpen;
       });

       details.hidden = true;
     });
   </script>
 </body>
